 "contents": "CK-1X single-seat jet cockpit: 24-facet (IML facets) white chamfered panel liner (20 mm, 8 mm seams) over the dark pressure-vessel liner, panelled fore / aft bulkheads, LED inlays; 5 canopy windows (tight black bezels, inner panes, shades); ejection-seat couch (black bucket, off-white cushions, catapult rails, yellow firing handle, harness, graphite pedestal); glass-cockpit main panel (3 MFDs with backlit bezel keys, guarded switch strip, black glare shield) + HUD combiner; left console with throttle quadrant, right console with sidestick, 4 switch plates; rudder pedals; 2 canopy-sill grab handrails (eqm48); ceiling LED inlays aft of the canopy",
 "notes": [
  "frame: crew posture gravity Godot -Z (aircraft level flight); the request said -Y gravity -> see the B9 frame flag",
  "R4: rear-hinged canopy (node_canopy_hinge Godot (0, -0.76, 0.7736) on the aft top edge, was (0, -0.75, 0.32) on the sill; axis +X, open 50 deg, front up): the liner is cut along the canopy cut line (planes y -0.75 / y 0.50 above the sill z 0.32, and the sill) with an 8 mm seam; the canopy-side liner pieces + the 5 window bezels / inner panes move with it (moving.canopy_interior)",
  "R3 checks: canopy swing sweep 0..50 deg vs the pilot envelope / furniture / fixed liner (checks.canopy_swing); egress / entry = seat envelope -> the open canopy opening (canopy liner ignored, harness straps / buckle released, need 0.6 m)",
  "no overhead panel: the canopy (windows 1-5) is overhead; the switch panels are on the side consoles",
  "all 5 canopy windows: tight 20 mm bezels with reveals opened along the eye sight lines (node_camera_1); main panel, glare shield and consoles clipped out of the eye -> clear-aperture cones; the HUD combiner (see-through glass on 2 posts) sits in the forward view by design"
 ],
